  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0018","idiomatic","In the twelfth year Dezong campaigned against the Xi and took seven thousand households.","In the twelfth year Dezu campaigned against the Xi and took seven thousand households.","Chinese 德祖 is the temple name Dezu; Dezong (德宗) is a different title, so the idiomatic misnames the campaigner.","high","applied"],
    ["s0018","literal","In the twelfth year Dezong attacked the Xi and captured seven thousand households.","In the twelfth year Dezu attacked the Xi and captured seven thousand households.","Chinese 德祖 is Dezu, not Dezong; the literal repeats the same wrong temple name.","high","applied"],
    ["s0020","idiomatic","In the fifth year of his reign the Taizu attacked western and eastern Xi, subdued them entirely, and held all the Xi and Mohe peoples.","In the fifth year of his reign the Taizu attacked western and eastern Xi, subdued them entirely, and held all the Xi and Xí peoples.","霫 denotes the Xí people, distinct from both the Xi (奚) and the Mohe (靺鞨); the worker's reading Ru was incorrect.","high","applied"],
    ["s0020","literal","In the fifth year of the Taizu's reign he attacked the western and eastern Xi, pacified them all, and wholly possessed the Xi and Mohe peoples.","In the fifth year of the Taizu's reign he attacked the western and eastern Xi, pacified them all, and wholly possessed the Xi and Xí peoples.","霫 denotes the Xí people, distinct from both the Xi (奚) and the Mohe (靺鞨); the worker's reading Ru was incorrect.","high","applied"]
  ],
